  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through Sunday)\nIssued at 308 PM CDT MON SEP 21 2026\n\nScattered convection with frequent lightning, heavy rainfall and\ngusty winds at times is being noted across the north central\nportions of Central Alabama ATTM. We have a 1 out of 5 risk for\nsevere storms this afternoon and evening and again on Tuesday\nafternoon and evening. The main threat is strong downburst winds,\nas well as heavy rain. The upper ridge of late is now confined to\nportions of Texas, Louisiana and Mexico. At the same time, an\nupper shortwave will continue to move EWD across the Dakotas and\ntoward the Great Lakes late by Tuesday. On Tuesday, guidance\nweakens/deteriorates the upper low over the Gulf Coast. However,\nrain chances continue for Tuesday, but instead will be focusing\non activity ahead of a cold front that should move through the\narea by Wednesday. Guidance continues to have a pattern shift\ntaking this front through the area and bringing much welcome more\n\"normal\" temperature readings for the second half of September\ninto Central Alabama for the latter half of the week and into\nthis weekend. There is a medium chance of seeing a few 50s in our\nnorthern counties starting on Friday and into the weekend, with\nlower to middle 60s elsewhere.\n\n08",
